# Predator Guard - environment template.
#
# Copy it to apps/web/.env.local: Next only loads env files from the app
# directory, so a .env in the repository root is silently ignored.
# NEVER put real keys in this file - it is tracked in git.

# ---- Vision model (what identifies the animal) ----
# The primary classifier: one key, one call per frame.
# Get a key at https://openrouter.ai/keys - unset => the app runs but the
# analyze endpoint answers 503 with setup instructions.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=replace-with-your-openrouter-token
# OPENROUTER_VISION_MODEL=minimax/minimax-m3.1-flash:free
# OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1

# ---- Database ----
# Postgres connection string. Omitted (or empty) => embedded PGlite (real
# Postgres compiled to WASM), so `npm run dev` needs no services at all.
# For a real server:  docker compose up -d db  and then
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://predator_guard:predator_guard@localhost:5432/predator_guard
# Neon PostgreSQL connection URI (safe template; replace <NEON_PASSWORD> locally/Vercel).
# Database: predator | Branch: production | SSL is required.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://neondb_owner:<NEON_PASSWORD>@ep-dark-night-b5nwrdd6-pooler.c-7.us-east-2.aws.neon.tech/predator?channel_binding=require&sslmode=require
# Where PGlite keeps its data directory (default: .pglite, gitignored).
# PGLITE_DATA_DIR=.pglite

# The current schema creates: farm_profile, cameras, detections, schema_migrations.
# Do not add credentials to this tracked file.
